ykeepers are a first paid caster role, not complete magic. Content depth, campaign counterplay and the full progression targets remain partial.Read the source for Gates B, F2 & J · A playable foundation↗Open gateGate C & integration · Remaining campaign proofThe land-commission source checkpoint passes 2,461 tests across 298 files in 67.00 seconds and all 74 local Pages cases in 5.3 minutes. Rules 37 AI uses an exact one-job allowance only when complete worked-cell quotes and unchanged worker proposals prove the same paid improvement as its strategic planner. Standard/Long/Epic headline outcomes remain 219/329/374 at twelve-realm seed 20260905, with 18/22/29 commission commands and no submitted or automatic refusals. These are turn-outcome comparisons, not identical full states or all-seed equivalence. Earlier adverse seeds were not rerun; Long remains late. DH-021 and all fifteen release gates remain open.Read the source for Gate C & integration · Remaining campaign proof↗Current / partialGate I · Orders across a large realmIndividual land commissions choose one improvement, a remaining total allowance and a treasury reserve. They can pay immediately, then answer after upkeep and charters; existing sites and mismatched extraction deposits stay protected. Successful direct construction/cultivation/cancellation ends a commission, while removal keeps already paid work. A generated two-worker hearth completes two paid fields by turn 7 with exact restoration. Group commissions, claims, cultivation and replacement strategy remain open. Worker stewardship adds Balanced, Food, Industry, Coin and Knowledge priorities for claimed land, immediate and post-growth allocation, explicit manual takeover and canonical waiting reasons. Up to 128 checked hearths can receive the same priority with named results; those worker priorities spend no coin and order no construction or land purchase. Checked land armies can receive shared patrol points while existing paused policies stay paused. Posting and charter requests bind to the reviewed campaign; uncertain publication requires saved restoration. Named receipts expose all accepted/refused actors through filtered 25-row pages without retrying orders or changing selection. Settlement order filters find empty queues, hearths without charters and waiting policies from supplied owned facts before 25-row paging, preserving checks outside the filter. Counts overlap; queued work comes first and a next-work candidate is not a guaranteed purchase. Six explicit charter changes restore an exact 36-record authored archive without altering queues or treasury. Group patrol controls pause, resume or remove existing policies across up to 128 checked land armies ashore, including checks outside the current filter. Issued travel is unchanged; unaffected and refused checks remain. Army registry order filters find postings, waiting reports and paused patrols before 25-row pagination while preserving checked IDs. Personal posting templates recall a policy before explicit group orders. Saved two-point land patrols respect direct routes, postings, voyages, missions and sieges. An AI seat can review a safe interrupted home leg or retire a narrowly observed captured-hearth circuit while preserving issued travel; player travel never resumes itself and ordinary player turns do not perform AI cleanup. Multi-step programs, escorts, broader governors and organic mature-empire acceptance remain unfinished.Read the source for Gate I · Orders across a large realm↗Open gateGates D, K & L · Scale and browser confidenceStorage publication performs O(prefix bytes) reads; queued-GC proof scans the store. Large-store GC, sustained memory, real quota/process-kill durability and cross-browser certification still need separate evidence. A still image is not a frame-time result.Read the source for Gates D, K & L · Scale and browser confidence↗Proposal / deferredSuggested follow-ups, not new release promisesPromoting the temporary storage probes to permanent regressions and separately profiling large-store GC are review suggestions. They require a bounded work packet and acceptance criteria. This journal does not authorize blocked probes or turn every suggestion into scope.Read the source for Suggested follow-ups, not new release promises↗Not this updateGate M, full magic and a 1.0 announcementNo online multiplayer service, complete magic system, new art production or overall 1.0 signoff is delivered here. Online play and full magical depth remain accepted release scope—not silently deferred out of 1.0. This journal adds a review surface, not those game systems.Read the source for Gate M, full magic and a 1.0 announcement↗Read all release gates →"
